K.5 Verification capacity frontier

Keyed to: Section 3.3, H2, Appendix C.

```
  P(missed correction)
    ^
    |                                     .----------  high load (ELR > 1)
    |                             .------'
    |                     .------'          <-- diminishing / flat returns
    |             .------'
    |       .-----'
    |  .----'                                .----------  low load (ELR < 1)
    | /                              .------'
    +------------------------------------------------> verification capacity V
                 V*  = capacity frontier

  Regions:

    ELR < 1   below frontier   added V reduces delay and reduces P(missed)
    ELR ~ 1   at frontier      added V reduces delay, small effect on P(missed)
    ELR > 1   above frontier   added V may fail to restore detection before T_c

  ELR = load / capacity
      = (decisions requiring review per unit time)
        / (decisions reviewable independently per unit time)
```

